<description>&lt;p&gt;Ecuadorian fishermen who survived US boat strikes are suing the United States for unlawful attacks, kidnapping and torture, while President Noboa continues to deny the existence of a US military base in the country. Prison gangs are expanding drug trafficking, illustrated by a man sentenced for fentanyl and heroin offenses, and the country is described as turning into a narco state. Violence against civilians persists, with a journalist murdered outside his home, two local election candidates shot dead in El Oro, and a priest killed when a crucifix fell during mass. The UCDP counted 2 battle-related deaths in 2019, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwgFBVV95cUxQZFFLRXdkUk9WMWJDc3RYTVhnYlZ2bEhVTGRqazJ6OEE5YVFFemtWa2dVdDU2ZG9ycGJkRkVzV1FrSDVaLVlJN1JSNmZpU1E0R29rc0lEbU1mRnVCMzN2aFE2RGNhUFU2cGM2Sm5Rc1liQ0pkNjVhQ1BoeEVBdUxRdzZpU005TDJpRS1GdUVlX2Z3bmZldG1WS2txOGhUMmFHeU5WRVhWclk5RnNyLTFJZUp2M0tOb1d2cTJYd3h6YmU3dw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiowFBVV95cUxPUkF6QTdlZlB3NDJJbVZ4VnVLSUdhcFF4WjRSOFpoWkhMcnc3RVZtZFE1OGQ5bWZQdHlxWlR0RFgxS1RobTY0RHhkUEpySm1NSVBQbnRnVDgzX2tYbkNpTU5YQXl4UmF0X2o4R3NqMjhsYWhHTk9oVTVtZ2oxbnV6UlFOcmpWdFkyU2cxX3huU21IUkhzLXRkRmpCMEtCYTJ3NWRN?oc=5&quot;&gt;Sri Lanka Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxPQVM2SEVWUXlCWC1sdTJqWlJ5Tm8wTUVmYW12UHRHZF81eGtTZ25sWWVoYXRZNVIxOWt3QVFjdmU4WndCblZKUE1Nd3h6U09aUWRMOExaQ25pMjU5OFFVMFZRYUJWMk1TMk0xMWI2LUpWcVZ3TUpwNlc3TExkR3dJSUUwOFBvRDliV3pRNWEzd0dLQUlSQmVoVVZ3?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiowFBVV95cUxPaGlTMEptZ2drRlRaTkFMN2RjZU5iOENmejhaeTZmQXAtNC10anZ4ZEVtVHBCOXFuSVMxb